        <type>std::vector&lt; T &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt; T &gt; micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::utility::split</definition>
        <argsstring>(T input, Delim_T delim)</argsstring>
        <name>split</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::utility::split</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>T</type>
          <declname>input</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Delim_T</type>
          <declname>delim</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Splits a string into a vector of sub-strings. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function template facilitates string handling in tests by splitting a string into a vector of substrings, using the specified delimiter.</para>
<para>The function iterates through the input string, identifying the positions of any of the delimiter characters (via <computeroutput>find_first_of()</computeroutput>) and extracting the substrings between them. Each non-empty substring is added to the output vector; empty substrings, such as those between consecutive delimiters, are omitted. This approach supports flexible parsing of delimited data, which is particularly useful for validating string processing logic in test cases.</para>
<para><bold>Example</bold></para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">namespace<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">mt<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(std::vector&lt;std::string_view&gt;{<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;b&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>==<sp/>mt::utility::split&lt;std::string_view&gt;<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a.b&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;.&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;a.b<sp/>splits<sp/>into<sp/>[a,b]&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the input string. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Delim_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the delimiter.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>input</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input string to split. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>delim</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Delimiter characters; any of them separates sub-strings. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A vector containing the resulting sub-strings; empty sub-strings (e.g. between consecutive delimiters) are omitted. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
